# Every Dockerfile in deploy/docker/ uses repo root as build context (`../../`)
# and no .dockerignore existed at all, so the ENTIRE working tree -- including
# whatever a developer happens to have lying around, like a locally run `npm
# install`/`pnpm install` -- was sent to BuildKit and available to COPY.
#
# This is the actual, confirmed root cause of deploy-demo-box's chronic build
# failure (16+ red runs since 2026-07-26, "cannot replace to directory
# .../node_modules/@opennextjs/cloudflare with file"): the demo box's checkout
# has a stray, root-owned apps/web-console/node_modules from a pnpm install
# run directly on the host (evidenced by pnpm-lock.yaml/.pnpm-store next to
# it), where node_modules/@opennextjs/cloudflare is a pnpm-style SYMLINK. Each
# Dockerfile's own `RUN npm install` step creates that same path as a REAL
# DIRECTORY inside the image first; the later `COPY apps/web-console/ ./`
# step then tried to overlay the host's symlink on top of it, and BuildKit's
# layer-diff-apply refuses to replace a directory with a file/symlink at the
# same path. Reproduced directly on the demo box, in isolation (a lone
# `web-console` build fails identically with zero concurrency), which rules
# out a build-concurrency race as the cause. Confirmed fixed by this file:
# excluding node_modules from the context means each image only ever sees the
# node_modules it installs for itself.
**/node_modules
**/.next
.git
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-store
